 ## Background
-The Signed Distance Function for a hexagonal prism is a standard primitive in ray marching and procedural modeling. It is derived from the geometry of a regular hexagon extruded along an axis. The formula in [S2, unofficial] is widely used in GLSL-based SDF libraries. The reflection-based approach in [S1, unofficial] is an alternative method that generalizes the distance calculation by mapping the point to a fundamental domain, which can be more numerically stable for very large or small coordinates but is computationally more expensive.
+Signed Distance Functions for primitives are widely used in ray marching for implicit surfaces. The hexagonal prism SDF is a standard primitive in libraries like [glsl-sdf-primitives](https://github.com/marklundin/glsl-sdf-primitives) [S2, unofficial] and [Torch-Sphere-Tracer](https://github.com/skmhrk1209/Torch-Sphere-Tracer) [S1, unofficial]. It is commonly used for modeling hex nuts, bolts, or honeycomb structures.
 
